2b2 (core g0.ts, beside WORD_CODES): refuse, as `metaprogramming`, an attribute named `init` or `builtin_init` wherever an attribute list names it:
- by canonical name, so `«init»` too;
- `@[init …]`;
- after a comma, `scoped` or `local` inside `@[…]`;
- `attribute [init …] x`.

The identifier `init` stays allowed everywhere else: `foldl (init := 0)`, a binder named `init`, `simp [init]`.

Tests in 2b2: those forms are refused; `(init := 0)` and `fun init => init` pass.

